# Abstract
# --------
# Assigns Git attributes to paths (https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes):
# the line ending normalisation, the diff drivers, the files stored in Git
# LFS, the files treated as binary, the linguist classification used for the
# GitHub language statistics and the paths left out of `git archive`.
#
# When several patterns match a path, the later line wins for each attribute.
# Git reads a `#` only at the start of a line as a comment, so every comment
# stands on its own line above the pattern it explains. Check the effect of a
# change with `git check-attr -a -- <path>`.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Store every text file with LF line endings in the repository, whatever the
# platform of the contributor. Git detects binary files automatically.
* text=auto eol=lf

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diff drivers: show the enclosing function or heading in diff hunks.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Show the enclosing Python function or class in hunk headers.
*.py diff=python
# Show the enclosing Markdown heading in hunk headers.
*.md diff=markdown
# Show the enclosing shell function in hunk headers for Bash scripts.
*.bash diff=bash
# Show the enclosing shell function in hunk headers for POSIX scripts.
*.sh diff=bash

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git LFS: model weights
# The starter weights of the model zoo are generated locally from the model
# id and are not committed (see src/unbihexium/zoo/catalog.yaml). Weight files
# that are committed anyway, for example fine-tuned checkpoints, are stored
# in Git LFS instead of the Git history.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Store ONNX models in Git LFS and never merge or diff them as text.
*.onnx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Store PyTorch checkpoints in Git LFS.
*.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Store PyTorch state dictionaries in Git LFS.
*.pth filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Store safetensors weight files in Git LFS.
*.safetensors filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary files tracked directly in Git
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# External tensor data of large ONNX models.
*.onnx.data binary
# NumPy arrays saved with numpy.save.
*.npy binary
# Compressed NumPy archives saved with numpy.savez.
*.npz binary
# PNG images in the documentation and tests.
*.png binary
# JPEG images with the .jpg extension.
*.jpg binary
# JPEG images with the .jpeg extension.
*.jpeg binary
# GIF images.
*.gif binary
# GeoTIFF rasters with the .tif extension.
*.tif binary
# GeoTIFF rasters with the .tiff extension.
*.tiff binary
# Icons, for example the documentation favicon.
*.ico binary
# PDF documents.
*.pdf binary

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub linguist
# Keep documentation, notebooks, model cards and licence texts out of the
# language statistics so that the repository is classified as Python.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Example notebooks count as documentation, not as Jupyter code.
examples/notebooks/*.ipynb linguist-documentation
# Model cards describe the model zoo and count as documentation.
model_zoo/cards/** linguist-documentation
# The documentation sources.
docs/** linguist-documentation
# Lock files written by `make lock` are generated and collapsed in diffs.
requirements*.txt linguist-generated

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# git archive: exclude development-only files from source archives
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .github/ stays in the archives: OpenSSF Scorecard reads the workflows from
# the GitHub source archive, and without them it cannot assess the
# Dangerous-Workflow, Token-Permissions, Pinned-Dependencies and Packaging
# checks. The sdist and the wheel are built by hatchling and do not use
# git archive.

# The pre-commit configuration is only used during development.
.pre-commit-config.yaml export-ignore

